{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused","id":1330104,"title":"Help Building an Air Aspected Melee Focused","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-09T12:10:59-07:00","id":1330104,"title":"Help Building an Air Aspected Melee Focused","content":"I'm building a character for an Dragon Blooded game next week and I'm feeling pretty overwhelmed by charms. <br /> <br /> He's a former Shinobi of Gens Karal who's wanted dead or alive by Lookshy and has been living in the lamb with his son in Chiarascuro for a few years. Sort of a Lone Wolf and Cub concept.<br /> <br /> The problem I'm having is that since 3E has come out, I struggle with grasping the power level of charms. I have no idea how effective double 9s or rerolled 6s are for example.<br /> <br /> I really could use some guidance. I'm mostly interested in Melee, Athletics, Larceny, Investigation, and Stealth charms. I'm also concerned about how all of these fire aura Melee charms are going to behave when I got bonfire in combat.<br /> <br /> Any help or advice would be greatly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T12:28:38-07:00","id":1330106,"title":"","content":"Very roughly, if you throw 10 dice you'll get about this many successes on average :<br /> <br /> no doubles : 4<br /> double 10 : 5<br /> double 9 : 6<br /> double 8 : 7<br /> double 7 : 8<br /> <br /> <u>when rerolling 6s :</u><br /> no doubles : 4<br /> double 10 : 5 or 6<br /> double 9 : 7<br /> double 8 : 8<br /> double 7 : 9","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:20:34-07:00","id":1330117,"title":"","content":"Don't use Melee. Use Ebon Shadow or Steel Devil or whatever other martial art depending on what weapon you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T13:32:28-07:00","id":1330120,"title":"","content":"I looked into making an Air-aspected swordsman, because I thought it was cool (and I had a load of inspiring art for it). It's not impossible, but I did find that, tbh, it's probably the worst aspect to use with Melee.<br /> <br /> I don't think that should entirely put you off, if you're really keen on it; you can just fight in Fire Aura (just don't go iconic) or use Balanced charms. And the Air signature charm is reasonable, when you reach Essence 3. But it's not a great choice.<br /> <br /> Still, making a character to be the most optimal rather than the cool vision you have in your head tends to lead to boring characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T14:01:42-07:00","id":1330127,"title":"","content":"Given House Tepet is (or was until recently) a House of legendary Air-Aspected warriors, you'd think melee wouldn't mix so poorly with the Air Aspect, but what can you do.<br /> <br /> One thing you could do is get the Horizon Cleaver Artifact and use its Evocations to cover the gaps the Melee tree has when you're Air Aspect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:13:33-07:00","id":1330143,"title":"","content":"This is so very disappointing news. I have this magnificent character concept and excellent backstory and now I feel like I'm going to be frustrated every time I'm stuck underperforming in combat, which if you've seen Lone Wolf and Cub is an essential aspect of the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:47:26-07:00","id":1330151,"title":"","content":"As BadassOverlord suggested Martial Arts trees can let you shine with Melee weapons just fine. I don't know Lone Wolf and Cub but a quick google tells me the Lone Wolf is a master of quick-draw swordsmanship, which is basically <b>Single Point Shining Into The Void</b> Style in a nutshell. Add a little Immaculate Air Style on the side so you can expend your Air Aura to remove Terrestrial Keywords and you'll probably have something decent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 08-09-2019, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:50:28-07:00","id":1330153,"title":"","content":"I do think the Air signature melee charm is good, IIRC, but the bonfire issue is significant.<br /> <br /> Have a look at some of the weapon-based martial arts. Even Blade (swords), White Reaper (spear), Wood Dragon (staff), Ebon Shadow (knives), etc. There might be something you like there, and they're all elementally-neutral.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:54:22-07:00","id":1330156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330127#post1330127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given House Tepet is (or was until recently) a House of legendary Air-Aspected warriors, you'd think melee wouldn't mix so poorly with the Air Aspect, but what can you do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.<br /> <br /> Though I did realise you can do something decent with Thrown in terms of front-line warriors. You always think of Thrown as being about assassins throwing shurikens (as that's what Solar thrown is like) but a lot of DB Thrown isn't necessarily that. There's quite a bit of stuff for piercing armour actually.<br /> And, unlike archery, a lot of thrown weapons are one-handed or can be used as melee weapons as well.<br /> <br /> So I think you can do your DB roman legionairre who leads in their front line and throws javelins (which, being artefact weapons, come back), then switches to melee when she gets charged.<br /> There's also of course the DB slinger leading the auxiliary slingers, but due to the way the Realm's military works, that's not a very prestigious position. Still, there's a lot of DBs per legion in a military house like Tepet.<br /> <br /> So that's what I imagine a lot of House Tepet's Air Aspects doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T15:54:56-07:00","id":1330157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330153#post1330153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think the Air signature melee charm is good, IIRC, but the bonfire issue is significant.<br /> <br /> Have a look at some of the weapon-based martial arts. Even Blade (swords), White Reaper (spear), Wood Dragon (staff), Ebon Shadow (knives), etc. There might be something you like there, and they're all elementally-neutral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even Blade? Is that 3E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T16:02:06-07:00","id":1330159,"title":"","content":"I created a Air Aspect Dragon-Blooded focused in Melee, but I need create two or three custom melee charms and use a custom silken black jade armor with thematics of fluid, harmony and evasion. I can send this things to you, but this character is not a starting DB.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-09T16:56:20-07:00","id":1330168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330156#post1330156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think you can do your DB roman legionairre who leads in their front line and throws javelins (which, being artefact weapons, come back), then switches to melee when she gets charged.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question is, why even switch back? At least for mechanical reasons close is the preferred range band for throwing weapons. For style points though I definitely agree, swap to melee.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, on to actual advice. In my opinion you have 3 options here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Option 1 Air Aura</span></u><br /> <br /> Compared to a lot of abilities melee is generous when it comes to balanced charms, so you can get away with just using them. You won't be as effective as a full fire aspect going melee, but you're not completely left out in the cold either. You've still got some neat tricks like Blinding Spark Distraction and the stacking melee excellency that will make you a deadly fighter, just not one of the greatest warriors ever. That can help you in your stealth though.<br /> <br /> Because you're never using a charm that will knock you out of Air Aura, you can sit in it the entire fight, which will eventually be useful for Vanishing Wind Body, the stealth charm that lets you ignore penalties for stealth in combat. If you did this it matters a lot less that you don't have a bunch of extra melee charms to throw into your attacks, because you're going to try really hard to stay out of high anima anyway. Also you might want to initiate combat, use Vanishing Wind Body, and then break your stealth by attacking the next turn. Also once you hit Essence 3 you can start muting your melee charms, letting you use bigger combos without flickering your anima.<br /> <br /> If you want to Shinobi assassinate somebody and then fade away into darkness, or just the one where you have to remember the least, that's probably the way to go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Option 2 Fire Aura</u></span><br /> <br /> If you want to though, you could try to use the full range of Fire options, this will give you damage adders and charms that let you protect somebody else, interposing yourself between them and an attacker, it will also open up the more powerful aura effects for you. For this you actually could retain a stealth angle, because you're going to need to stop yourself from going bonfire and knocking you out of fire aura.<br /> <br /> This opens up some more tactical options for you, for example the damage adder Crimson Fang Bite becomes available. You won't be able to full excellency with it all the time, so it's better against low defense but high soak enemies, which can also make it good as a big assassin alpha strike. You'll also open up great charms like Burning Pinnacle Strike, and get full effect from the Warden section of the tree.<br /> <br /> You'll be a pretty good brawler and a great protector, so if you really want to keep safe your little cub I'd say go this route. If you do though make sure your stats are very high, strength, dex, and melee, with a specialty or even two, just to make sure your accuracy is good and you're getting the most out of your charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><u><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Option 3 No Aura</span></u></span><br /> <br /> With this option you just take whatever charm, don't care about aura, don't care about anima level. Don't take any charms that require aura, and don't even read the aura effects of charms. Use Flame Borne Interception to parry, Graceful Flowing Defense to ignore a penalty, and then attack on your turn with Demon Crushing Wolf Bite to get past the enemy's crazy high soak, or Crimson Fang Bite to lay on extra hurt on a low soak enemy.<br /> <br /> With this option you'll be less efficient, getting bang for your motes than other styles, but also a lot more versatile. Flame Warden Stance isn't awful without the aura bonus, it's still perfectly usable as a charm to defend other your son for the whole scene, and Blazing Interception's aura effect doesn't even do anything unless your charge is rolled into combat.<br /> <br /> This is probably the least challenging way to play, but it's also the most charm and mote intensive. You want a lot of charms to take advantage of the fact that you're not limiting yourself to what you can use.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u>Option 4 Do Them All</u></span><br /> <br /> Or you could just go crazy and get an absolute metric ton of charms and pick the style you think suits the situation. Are you fleeing the city, protecting your son and need to make it REALLY clear to anyone chasing you that attacking him is a bad idea? Go Fire Aura and end the first person that tries to hurt him with one decisive slash. Need to do a shadow shinobi assassination? Go Air Aura and stealth your way deep into enemy territory with Soaring Zephyr Flight, and then fade back into the shadows. Doing either of those and it's not going to plan? Drop the aura and unleash the full power of all five elements at once.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also in any of these cases evocations will probably help you get more of an edge, so definitely take a look at some artifacts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, I know that's really complicated, and to be honest I probably missed at least one thing, but hopefully that helps guide you a bit!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T01:56:41-07:00","id":1330221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330157#post1330157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even Blade? Is that 3E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooops! Sorry, I meant Single Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T02:52:37-07:00","id":1330227,"title":"","content":"<i>My sign does not lie.</i><br /> <br /> Air Aspects speak to me more than any other type of Exalted. I want to help you, because I've put countless hours into trying to build this. I'll try to save you what frustration I can.<br /> <br /> <i>But I would have had BB!</i><br /> <br /> Martial Arts has been suggested. It's not a bad suggestion. Martial Arts charms are generally balanced around the level of Terrestrial charms. Single Point has a very <i>Shogun Assassin</i> feel, whilst Steel Devil is a bit more <i>Kill Bill</i>. Ebon Shadow gives you a surpising number of &quot;melee&quot; options and whilst Itto is famous for his d\u014dtanuki, he does use other weapons. And if we're considering other weapons there's a great fight in the manga where he uses guns and a halberd (Righteous Devil/White Reaper).<br /> <br /> The problem with martial arts is two fold:<br /> <br /> 1. The Terrestrial keyword. This nerfs Single Point into the Void. The style is completely unusable with the Terrestrial keyword. It's not a matter of being mechanically suboptimal: it's completely worthless and deeply frustrating. Other styles aren't so bad (even White Reaper), the keyword isn't such a great nerf and it can be managed with Aura.<br /> <br /> 2. Armor. Much more serious, Terrestrials don't have the same damage mitigation options as Solars and Lunars. A lack of Hardness and Penalty negation opens you up to alpha strikes. And Evocations are excellent (go look at Mela's Coil, you want your Swordsman to Rush at Medium Range and have <i>Uniform</i> +5 Damage? Sure you do!). Martial Arts is sucking down four merit points which you could be spending on Artifact armor AND it's locking you out of using armor. That's... well that's a death sentence. Fortunately, if you like the idea of Martial Arts then there are options. A Belt of Shadow Walking syngergises great with Air abilities, and there's Silken Armor. (Invulnerable Skin of Bronze also gives a passive soak bonus as a control option, and when summoned only counts as Medium armor, so that's worth considering on any Martial Arts build.)<br /> <br /> <i>When I was little, my father was famous. He was the greatest Samurai in the Empire...</i><br /> <br /> If you want generic sword fighter advice, I have a couple of builds that might inspire you.<br /> <br /> Builds: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314291-help-me-design-the-invincible-sword-dynast?p=1314551#post1314551\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...51#post1314551</a> (You can also find a reasonable breakdown of the Melee and Athletics charms in that thread.)<br /> <br /> My advice is to grab Mela's Coil, a good artifact sword and invest heavily in Evocations. Use Balanced and Air melee charms. (DrLoveMonkey's Option 1.)<br /> <br /> But most importantly, winning the character creation minigame will buy you slack for suboptimal choices in play.<br /> <br /> Generic character creation minigame advice: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322405-exalted-3e-need-the-advice-help-of-the-mechanics-savvy-folks?p=1322493#post1322493\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...93#post1322493</a><br /> <br /> For the general dice trick charms, the (extremely) short-hand is that each trick (double 9s, reroll 6s) is worth one success. You usually want to max your dicepool first (with an Excellency usually) and throw on the dice tricks second.<br /> <br /> <i>President John Adams.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-11-2019, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T03:24:01-07:00","id":1330229,"title":"","content":"Even two more home brew air aspect melee charms would probably make a big difference. Do you have two ideas of particularly air like melee abilities?<br /> <br /> Edit : Or, apparently, shadowninja has a few for you to look at up thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","user":"Apromor","date":". 08-10-2019, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T06:23:50-07:00","id":1330238,"title":"","content":"Sorry for double post. Browser problems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","user":"Timbo","date":". 08-10-2019, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T08:08:43-07:00","id":1330249,"title":"","content":"Okay, so my plan was to try to use fire aura for Melee pretty much all of the time and dump anima with Smoldering Essence Attack but I'm pretty sure they 5m cost is actually going to cause be to stay essence neutral, so I'll have to use it everytime I want to spend more than 5 essence once I hit burning anima. Is that right? They seems incredibly expensive.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"437\" data-vbnamecard=\"437\">shadowninja</a> (or anyone really) I would absolutely love to see and get feedback on some custom melee are charms that would help around out the tree for an air aspected melee user. Is anyone has any that I could show to my ST after vetting them here, I'd be very grateful.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, your post is amazing and it makes me feel like my concept isn't hopeless. Though, I feel like I'm going to feel like I'm working too hard when my Earth Aspected friend is just effortlessly whomping everything with Fist of the Titans and Earth Dragon Style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","user":"Timbo","date":". 08-10-2019, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T10:09:51-07:00","id":1330265,"title":"","content":"This is my custom charms:<br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Wind Cutting Attack</span></b><br /><br /> <b>Cost: </b>4m (+2i); <b>Mins: </b>Melee 4, Essence 2; <b>Type: </b>Supplemental; <b>Keywords: </b>Air; <b>Duration: </b>Instant; <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Crimson Fang Bite<br /> Channeling the essence of air Dragon-Blooded is able to project your weapon's attacks on the Short Range. <b>Withering</b> attacks can be performed normally, but <b>Decisive</b> attacks require the additional expense of two Initiative points.<br /> In air aura, attacks can be performed up to Medium Range without requiring Aim action. <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Freezing Essence Attack</span></b><br /><br /> <b>Cost: </b>\u2014; <b>Mins: </b>Melee 5, Essence 3; <b>Type: </b>Permanent; <b>Keywords: </b>Air; <b>Duration: </b>Permanent; <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Smoldering Essence Attack<br /> The Dragon-Blooded learns how to channel the essence of Air through your weapon, freezing your enemies. This charm modifies <i>Smoldering Essence Attack</i>, which loses the <i>Fire</i> keyword and gains the <i>Air/Fire</i> keyword. If you use the Air version, the basic effect of the charm is modified: Instead of burning the opponent, the charm freezes him, causing a (Essence) penalty on physical actions (half that value in Evasion and Parry, rounded up) and suffers (Essence) damage with <b>Withering</b> without Soak. This effect lasts for one turn plus one additional turn per every 10 in the <b>Withering</b> attack's damage roll or until the target succeeds in a <b>Withering</b> attack against Dragon-Blooded. <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Swift Precision Strike</span></b><br /><br /> <b>Cost: </b>\u2014; <b>Mins: </b>Melee 5, Essence 3; <b>Type: </b>Permanent; <b>Keywords: </b>Air; <b>Duration: </b>Permanent; <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Burning Pinnacle Strike<br /> Using the lightness and speed of the essence of Air, Dragon-Blooded is able to accelerate its attacks. This charm modifies Burning Pinnacle Strike, which loses the <i>Fire</i> keyword and gains the <i>Air/Fire</i> keyword. In addition, you can pay for the activation of the charm with initiative, 3i instead of 3m.<br /> <br /> I created many other charms to my exalted campaing (you can access my file in this <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1fvxsbo22oGzi9xlbhOGQC7jVtbz30K4A/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">link</a>), the majority of then are in Portuguese (I am from Brazil), but you can use the <a href=\"https://translate.google.com.br/?hl=pt-BR&amp;tab=rT\" target=\"_blank\">Google Translator</a> to help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/437-shadowninja","name":"shadowninja","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"62"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T10:56:41-07:00","id":1330273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330249#post1330249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though, I feel like I'm going to feel like I'm working too hard when my Earth Aspected friend is just effortlessly whomping everything with Fist of the Titans and Earth Dragon Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to every Dragon-Blooded build that isn't Fire Swordsman, Air Ninja, Wood Archer, Water Pugilist or (Element) Immaculate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadowninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330265#post1330265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my custom charms:</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm all for custom charms, but this approach of &quot;this DB charm but a different aspect&quot; where you still have to buy the original ends up feeling like you're paying extra xp to do the same another player can do by playing the &quot;right&quot; aspect.<br /> <br /> I'd say picking a 5-dot Blue Jade artifact so you can give it as many Evocations as you want and using mainly that is the least headache-inducing way to do this. And it might even turn out more powerful to boot since Resonant Evocations are supposed to be a step up from DB native charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T11:04:28-07:00","id":1330274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330249#post1330249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so my plan was to try to use fire aura for Melee pretty much all of the time and dump anima with Smoldering Essence Attack but I'm pretty sure they 5m cost is actually going to cause be to stay essence neutral, so I'll have to use it everytime I want to spend more than 5 essence once I hit burning anima. Is that right? They seems incredibly expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not actually 100% sure this works. If the 5m cost for Smorldering Essence Attack is coming out of your peripheral mote pool, I think you might just be spending a level of anima only to get it right back. It's not useless though, it means if you have a level of anima you can use it and 4 other motes and not pop up a level.<br /> <br /> Managing anima can be frustrating, and while it's not impossible it does stop you from doing anything really explosive more than once or twice. You CAN do it by carefully metering out your peripheral essence pool, like only spend 4m out of it for join battle, only raise your parry through peripheral by 2, ect. You can also do things like use Portenteous Comet Deflection as long as you don't excellency the crap out of the clash attack. Good news though! If you're only fighting one opponent the Melee excellency discount will stack up to make full exellency attacks possible! Also if you don't excellency a lot of attacks, there are very few melee charms that cost more than 4 motes, so activating any one of those on its own is fine.<br /> <br /> Then after a turn or two of that, especially if you haven't punched up your anima at all, you can cut completely loose and blow all of your personal motes as well as anything left in the tank from your peripherals on a series of overpowered attacks. It can also fit a certain type of samurai aesthetic where you're holding back, holding back, holding back and then controlled release to end your opponents. There's even a neat trick you can do at Essence 4, if you ever get there, where you do all that, explode into bonfire with your last attack, which swaps you instantly to Air Aura, and then next turn you can use Mela's Flashing Tongue to make a bunch of withering attacks and one decisive in a single turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are some problems with that style though. For one if you're facing a truly deadly opponent in a duel then your restraint in the first half of combat could get you killed. In that case I say go as hard as you can with personal, then when you get to peripheral if you're not ready to end the fight try shaving off enough motes that you only spend 4-9-14 in a single instant so that you don't peak more anima than you have to, and then when you're backed into a corner trigger Harnessed Firestorm Assault and try to end the fight, or at least put them in their -4s or something.<br /> <br /> After that you lose Burning Pinnacle Strike, Smoldering Essence Attack, and the really good benefit of Portenteous Comet Deflection,, and Harnessed Firestorm Assault, which are the only ones that really matter in that kind of instance. That won't necessarily spell a death sentence, but it sucks, and you need to make that buildup count. Also that only works if you start the fight with full personal motes anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing to consider is your ST, because there's a lot out there, my former self included, who don't like putting in fights against opponents that aren't super skilled and really deadly. I don't think it's necessarily the wrong way to play the game if everyone is having fun, but I don't like it anymore personally. In which case managing your motes by using charms without full excellencies is going to feel really bad. It's just hard to hit somebody with a parry of 11 and onslaught penalty negators without going full attack, and that doesn't fit your character.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if you're facing more reasonable things with a parry of like, 4-5 without penalty negators, and you maxed out your stats then you can easily just use 1 mote or 0 mote excellencies combined with the fun charms like Burning Pinnacle Strike, or Smoldering Essence. Remember though to use Smoldering Essence you need at least one anima level, so maybe full excellency your join battle or first attack or something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330249#post1330249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1121_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1121\" data-vbnamecard=\"1121\">DrLoveMonkey</a>, your post is amazing and it makes me feel like my concept isn't hopeless. Though, I feel like I'm going to feel like I'm working too hard when my Earth Aspected friend is just effortlessly whomping everything with Fist of the Titans and Earth Dragon Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah Earth Dragon is one of the most straightforwardly powerful options for DBs. As an Earth Aspect using it you CAN get a lot more out of it by being clever, but if all you do is stand there and hit things you'll do just fine. The only real advantage you have over him by doing the Fire Aura style of fighting is that because you're really throttling your motes back, over successive fights or even long fights you're going to have a lot left for the final battle.<br /> <br /> If there's 2-3 action scenes in one, I dunno, palace assault or something lets say, and your friend full excellencies every join battle, every attack, every defense, and boosts them all with as many charms and evocations as he can, then he'll end fights fast and be out halfway through the second one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-10T16:40:16-07:00","id":1330316,"title":"","content":"Actually put a hold in what I just said, I need to run some tests to see if it actually feels okay or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T04:10:38-07:00","id":1330366,"title":"","content":"<i>You would've been happier if you'd chosen to join your mother in her world.</i><br /> <br /> Here's my unsoliticted advice.<br /> <br /> Swordplay is not &quot;in Aspect&quot; for Airs. Neither is Larceny and Investigation. You can do both, but splitting focus that much means you're not going to be good at both. If you want to be good at both you need to be looking at Water or Fire Aspects. I've dropped Larceny and Investigation from this sample build.<br /> <br /> <i>When you hold a Hattori Hanzo sword, you compare it to every sword ever made, that was not made by Hattori Hanzo.</i><br /> <br /> Itto wields a practical battle-sword in an era where decorative, stylized weapons are the norm. Now Shining Ice Mirror is a simple, practical katana, but I don't think it's a good fit. In the manga (and films) his sword attracts everything from condescending curiosity to pants-wetting-terror: it's an ugly weapon built to kill, a weapon of war in a time of peace. For me, I think Gorgon translates this well.<br /> <br /> I threw on a warboomerang. Javelins, short spears or hatchets work just as well.<br /> <br /> <i>At night, we make a fire, and have our tea, and we listen for the ninja, who never make a sound.</i><br /> <br /> Add in my generic advice for maximizing XP and you get something like this:<br /> <br /> Shogun Assassin Character Sheet:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Karal Ito<br /> Air Aspect<br /> Ronin Swordsman<br /> <br /> Strength 5<br /> Dexterity 5<br /> Stamina 1<br /> <br /> Charisma 1<br /> Manipulation 1<br /> Appearance 5<br /> <br /> Perception 3<br /> Intelligence 1<br /> Wits 5<br /> <br /> Air Aspect Abilities (and Specialities)<br /> <br /> Linguistics 1<br /> Lore 3 (Lookshy Politics)<br /> Occult 5<br /> Stealth 5<br /> Thrown 3<br /> <br /> Favoured Abilities<br /> <br /> Athletics 5 (Rushes)<br /> Awareness 5 (Join Battle)<br /> Integrity 5 (My honour is my life)<br /> Melee 5 (Swords)<br /> Resistance 5<br /> <br /> Merits (Native Language: Rivertongue)<br /> <br /> Artifact 5 (Mela's Coil)<br /> Artifact 5 (Gorgon)<br /> Artifact 3 (Belt of Shadow Walking)<br /> Pain Tolerance<br /> (Gens Freebie) Retainer 2 (Karal Dagor\u014d)<br /> (Gens Freebie) Language (Flametongue)<br /> (Gens Freebie) Language (Old Realm)<br /> (Gens Freebie) Resources 1 (Ronin for Hire)<br /> <br /> Free Excellencies<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Effortlessly Rising Flame<br /> 2. Awareness: Precision Awareness Method<br /> 3. Melee: Stoking Bonfire Style<br /> 4. Stealth: Distracting Breeze Technique<br /> 5. Thrown: Seeking Throw Technique<br /> <br /> Charms<br /> <br /> 1. Athletics: Soaring Leap Technique<br /> 2. Melee: Flame-Borne Interception<br /> 3. Melee: Blinding Spark Distraction<br /> 4. Melee: Crossfire Flash<br /> 5. Occult: Spirit Detecting Mirror<br /> 6. Occult: Spirit Grounding Shout<br /> 7. Resistance: Oxbody Technique<br /> 8. Resistance: Oxbody Technique x2<br /> 9. Resistance: Oxbody Technique x3<br /> 10. Resistance: Oxbody Technique x4<br /> 11. Resistance: Oxbody Technique x5<br /> <br /> Evocations<br /> <br /> 12. Mela's Coil: Wind Rider Swiftness<br /> 13. Gorgon: Stone-sinew Offensive<br /> 14. Gorgon: Granite Venom Strike<br /> 15. Gorgon: Life-devouring Hellion Blade<br /> <br /> Intimacies<br /> <br /> Defining Principle: Without honour a man is nothing<br /> Defining Tie: Karal Dagoro, my son (paternal love)<br /> Major Principle: The Immaculate Faith (Loyal Adherence)<br /> Major Tie: Gens Karal (Vengeance)<br /> Minor Tie: Anathema (Disgust)<br /> Minor Principle: Sword for hire, son for hire<br /> <br /> Bonus Points<br /> Taking 7 abilities from 3 to 5 (14)<br /> Merits 4<br /> <br /> Evasion 3<br /> Parry 7<br /> Soak 12 Hardness 10<br /> Mobility Penalty -0<br /> <br /> Gorgon Attacks Accuracy 14 (11 Decisive), Damage 17 (Overwhelming 5), Lethal, Chopping, Wakefulness<br /> <br /> Razor Claws Accuracy 10 (5 Decisive), 15 Damage (OVR 3), Lethal, Concealable, Worn<br /> <br /> Warboomerang Accuracy 12/11/10 (8 Decisive), 14 Damage (OVR 1), Thrown (Medium), Lethal, Cutting, Returns<br /> <br /> Join Battle 11 (+3 to result)<br /> Rush 11<br /> Disengage 5<br /> <br /> Resolve 5 (6)<br /> Guile 1<br /> <br /> Willpower 5<br /> Essence 2<br /> <br /> Personal motes 13<br /> Peripheral motes 31 (15, 16 committed)<br /> <br /> Health Track<br /> -0 x1<br /> -1 x14<br /> -3 x1<br /> Incap<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> Tactics:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The idea is to stay Balanced and use Evocations as your combat workhorse. You're good at Stealth, Awareness, Athletics. You've got a ranged option if you need it. You don't completely suck at intellectual pursuits (especially if you can stunt thinking on your feet). You are a straightforward and forthright warrior... which plays socially as you'd expect.<br /> <br /> You suffer from a limited mote pool and a lack of Onslaught negation.<br /> <br /> You want to spend WP to wake Gorgon. Wind Rider's Swiftness to close in. Then Excellency and Stone-sinew to lock your target down. The Belt stops you getting mobbed by mortals. You want to pick on battle groups first to build Initiative and Wakefulness.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Edit (My Builds):<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1314291-help-me-design-the-invincible-sword-dynast?p=1314551#post1314551\">Starting Character Sword Fighter - The Invincible Sword Dynast</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330366#post1330366\">Starting Character - Air Aspect Shogun Assassin</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322405-exalted-3e-need-the-advice-help-of-the-mechanics-savvy-folks?p=1324494#post1324494\">Best Possible 175 XP Combat Build - The Invincible</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1322405-exalted-3e-need-the-advice-help-of-the-mechanics-savvy-folks?p=1325509#post1325509\">Drafts</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 02-14-2020, 06:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T04:31:51-07:00","id":1330370,"title":"","content":"Is there a particular reason for Appearance 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T05:38:15-07:00","id":1330374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330370#post1330370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a particular reason for Appearance 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Short answer? No.<br /> Long answer?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Shogun Assassin here is based on The Invincible Sword Dynast, which uses Appearance on War rolls to command her troops as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/768056-is-appearance-kind-of-rubbish-or-am-i-missing-something?p=769441#post769441\">Appearance is objectively better than Charisma</a>.<br /> <br /> From a simple XP efficiency point of view 5/1/1 is the best array. And being able to make 5 dice social rolls is better than three and two dice rolls.<br /> <br /> The Itto from Lone Wolf and Cub isn't exactly renown for his charisma or his skill at manipulating people. He's a hard bitten headsman.<br /> <br /> And Tomisabur\u00f4 Wakayama is my type.<br /> <br /> It's just a sample build. Change anything you don't like. (13 dots of artifacts.)</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T08:07:43-07:00","id":1330383,"title":"","content":"It's crazy that every single build here assumes that every player can just take as many of any artifacts they can spend for. I've had three different STs and that were all super controlling of artifacts.<br /> <br /> Hell, I've been denied Sorcery and Martial Arts with most of my characters. Honestly, I wasn't even allowed to take Single Point Shining Into the Void unless I made it the central theme of my concept which means no Immaculate Dragon Style to make it work well.<br /> <br /> Hell, my concept was originally thought up as an Air Aspect, If I change it now, 3 days before my first session, I'll surely catch hell for it. I'm not complaining mind you, after all I got an exclusive invite to play a really cool game with my friends.<br /> <br /> My point is that when I see all these min-maxed builds with unrealistic ability spreads, I have a hard time taking them seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T09:07:25-07:00","id":1330390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330383#post1330383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that when I see all these min-maxed builds with unrealistic ability spreads, I have a hard time taking them seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Corebook provides the basic rules for playing the game.<br /> <br /> I'm afraid I have no way of knowing how an individual ST will change the rules of the game.<br /> <br /> This isn't to say STs shouldn't change the rules, merely that I can only give advice based on what the <i>actual</i> rules allow. <br /> <br /> I'm happy to give advice based on houserules (which is why I made the 175XP builds) if you tell me what the houserules are.<br /> <br /> Likewise, custom charms and artifacts. I wouldn't allow any of shadowninja's custom charms (Melee atracks at medium range without aiming? Really?), but obviously shadowninja's ST is fine with it. As Mela's Coil incorporates a 3-dot artifact as part of it's attunement bonus, an argument could be made for swapping the Razor Claws for a built in Belt of Shadow Walking: but again, I have no idea how that would fly with individual STs.<br /> <br /> As to restricting martial arts... I don't know how to respond to that. I'm glad your ST allowed you to branch out, I guess. (The actual rules of the game let you take martial arts and it doesn't have to define your character.)<br /> <br /> I'd love your feedback on how Single Point works out for you in play, and what kind of foes you face in your game. And I'd love to see the character you will be playing with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T10:26:39-07:00","id":1330404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330383#post1330383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is that when I see all these min-maxed builds with unrealistic ability spreads, I have a hard time taking them seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually this is something I wanted to bring up. Do you want your character to be powerful enough to easily fight ten elite soldiers and their captain without breaking a sweat, or do you want to be the kind of character that makes even other exalted design themselves to death if they face you?<br /> <br /> The latter takes a really hard and focused build that doesn\u2019t really leave a lot of space for other things, but by Essence 3-4 just about the only things you\u2019ll worry about fighting are Celestial exalted and second circle demons. The former will not be quite so good, and if your friend is going full maximum power earth immaculate you\u2019ll probably feel like you\u2019re not keeping up, but depending on the fights your ST faces you off against you\u2019re still going to feel like a badass and be able to diversify your build a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T11:25:51-07:00","id":1330414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330404#post1330404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually this is something I wanted to bring up. Do you want your character to be powerful enough to easily fight ten elite soldiers and their captain without breaking a sweat, or do you want to be the kind of character that makes even other exalted design themselves to death if they face you?<br /> <br /> The latter takes a really hard and focused build that doesn\u2019t really leave a lot of space for other things, but by Essence 3-4 just about the only things you\u2019ll worry about fighting are Celestial exalted and second circle demons. The former will not be quite so good, and if your friend is going full maximum power earth immaculate you\u2019ll probably feel like you\u2019re not keeping up, but depending on the fights your ST faces you off against you\u2019re still going to feel like a badass and be able to diversify your build a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>They latter build definitely. The cub in my Lone Wolf and Cub concept is anathema so I'm definitely going to have to be able to handle other exalts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T11:47:27-07:00","id":1330419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330414#post1330414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They latter build definitely. The cub in my Lone Wolf and Cub concept is anathema so I'm definitely going to have to be able to handle other exalts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the former build can fight exalts, but you\u2019ll be fighting them on a much more even footing, at least as long as your ST is using antagonists similar to the ones in the book and not designing max-stat all-charms enemies. <br /> <br /> But that\u2019s the thing, you\u2019ll be on a mostly even footing, you\u2019ll still have an edge on them but especially if you don\u2019t have artifacts it\u2019s going to be small. If you want to be the type of character that eats exalted warriors for breakfast then you\u2019re going to pretty much need to focus on that and nothing else. You really need melee, dodge, resistance, athletics, awareness, and occult, most of them at 5 with applicable specialties and several charms, it just won\u2019t leave room for anything else until like Essence 4 or something. With that you will be one of the greatest fighters in the world stronger than almost anything, but even with that you\u2019re not going to be able to go 1v3 against other warriors, so keep in mind that you\u2019re not invincible either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T12:19:24-07:00","id":1330422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330419#post1330419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, the former build can fight exalts, but you\u2019ll be fighting them on a much more even footing, at least as long as your ST is using antagonists similar to the ones in the book and not designing max-stat all-charms enemies. <br /> <br /> But that\u2019s the thing, you\u2019ll be on a mostly even footing, you\u2019ll still have an edge on them but especially if you don\u2019t have artifacts it\u2019s going to be small. If you want to be the type of character that eats exalted warriors for breakfast then you\u2019re going to pretty much need to focus on that and nothing else. You really need melee, dodge, resistance, athletics, awareness, and occult, most of them at 5 with applicable specialties and several charms, it just won\u2019t leave room for anything else until like Essence 4 or something. With that you will be one of the greatest fighters in the world stronger than almost anything, but even with that you\u2019re not going to be able to go 1v3 against other warriors, so keep in mind that you\u2019re not invincible either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which charms? Also, what's all of the Occult for? Spirit-whomping? Is it necessary that I have these? Apparently multiple players are doing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","user":"Timbo","date":". 08-11-2019, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T21:34:45-07:00","id":1330486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330422#post1330422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which charms? Also, what's all of the Occult for? Spirit-whomping? Is it necessary that I have these? Apparently multiple players are doing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, either that or the three dot artifact that makes you a dematerialized wraith that can still attack non-dematerialized targets. (so a defensive pick)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T22:29:09-07:00","id":1330490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330422#post1330422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Welll...a lot of charms. Here's a basic rundown, I think, of the ones you want for fighting, assuming you want to go with the Fire Aura idea and no artifacts and stuff.<br /> <b>Athletics</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (1)Effortlessly Rising Flame: You want this to chase down fleeing archers with rushes, otherwise they might just stay at range from you and kill you from there.<br /> <br /> (1)Bellows Pumping Stride: More bonuses to rushes.<br /> <br /> (1)Soaring Leap Technique: More bonuses to rushes and disengages.<br /> <br /> (1)Verdant Dragon Footsteps: This charm lets you ignore penalties for moving in heavily wooded areas, which you might have to fight in.<br /> <br /> (3)Dancing Ember Stride: Actually moving into short range instantly after rushing, very good.<br /> <br /> (3)Inescapable Blazing Advance: Again more bonuses to rushes and also sets your enemy ablaze.<br /> <br /> (5)Falling Star Maneuver: Allows you to make a reflexive attack after instantly rushing, which is also a shockwave, so good AoE plus reflexive attack, even if it counts as your combat action.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Awareness</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (1)Precision Observation Method: This is for boosting your Join Battle so you can go first, have more initiative in combat, spot ninja assassins creeping up on you, detect poisons, the list goes on and on.<br /> <br /> (1)Cloud-Piercing Focus: You want this just in case you have to fight in a fog or sandstorm or something, but more importantly it's a pre-requisite.<br /> <br /> (1)Deep Listening Palm: Not really useful in fighting, but useful as a pre-requisite.<br /> <br /> (1)All Encompassing Earth Sense: This charm triggers when you get within short range of somebody dangerous, like a Realm or Lookshy assassin, it's good for avoiding ambushes.<br /> <br /> (2)Feeling the Dragon's Bones: Another good charm for feeling out attackers or ambushes, but more useful as a pre-req.<br /> <br /> (2)Dragon's Crushing Gaze: Directly gives you what is essentially a non-charm success for ferreting out a disguised or hidden target.<br /> <br /> (3)Dragon's Twitching Whisker: Super useful, if somebody hates you and gets anywhere near you, you'll know to get ready for a fight.<br /> <br /> (3)Eye of Blazing Truth: This charm will let you pick out an ambusher, deal some damage to them, and force them from their hiding place, so it's good to have.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you have all of those charms you will have done basically everything you can charm-wise to make sure nobody will ever get the drop on you, and will regret it if they try.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Dodge</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> (1)Threshold Warding Stance: You won't be able to block everything, some attacks are just unblockable, so you want this just in case. Also if you're fighting 2 enemies at once you can keep building your melee excellency discount on one while dodging the other. Also if you ever need to disengage, you need doge.<br /> <br /> (1)Heat of Battle Advance: Solid mobility charm for chasing down archers even if you're in the midst of a melee. You might have to do this when faced with an exalted archer and his battlegroup of mortal soldiers.<br /> <br /> (1)Flickering Candle Meditation: A decent charm, and also a pre-req for everything else.<br /> <br /> (2)Hopping Firecracker Evasion: A charm that lets you disengage reflexively and for free if you beat the attack by 2 successes.<br /> <br /> (2)Ember Amid Smoke Misdirection: Punish foes for missing you.<br /> <br /> (3)Unassailable Body of Fire: Punish people even more.<br /> <br /> (3)Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion: Punish them EVEN more for missing.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Melee</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <br /> (1)Stoking Bonfire Style: It's the melee excellency, you want it.<br /> <br /> (1)Flame Borne Interception: Good at raising defense against multiple opponents.<br /> <br /> (1)Blinding Spark Distraction: Blinding your opponent will let you hit them easier and make yourself harder to hit, you want it too.<br /> <br /> (1)Burning Fury Wreath: It's an essential pre-req and ignoring hardness can be helpful in a pinch.<br /> <br /> (2)Elemental Sheath: Never be caught unarmed.<br /> <br /> (2)Dragon Graced Weapon: REALLY never be caught unarmed and also add bonuses to your weapon.<br /> <br /> (2)Crimson Fang Bite: It's a damage adder that will help you crash enemies<br /> <br /> (2)Demon Crushing Wolf Bite: It sacrifices your fire aura, but facing against a foe with insane soak it might be useful.<br /> <br /> (2)Flame Warden Stance: The defend other charm to protect your cub.<br /> <br /> (2)Blazing Interception: Counterattack people who are attacking your ward.<br /> <br /> (2)Crossfire Flash: If you're ever in a a clash this is a good non-charm die adder.<br /> <br /> (3)Root and Hand Merging: A balanced charm that gives you a permanent parry increase.<br /> <br /> (3)Dragon Soul Burst: Decent charm to use if you have time to aim to get free damage<br /> <br /> (3)Smoldering Essence Attack: After your attack lands you keep hurting your opponent.<br /> <br /> (3)Buring Pinnacle Strike: It's free reflexive attacks, they're good.<br /> <br /> (3)Portenteous Comet Deflection: It's more reflexive attacks.<br /> <br /> (3)Fire Incites Water to a Riot of Clouds: ANOTHER reflexive attack!<br /> <br /> (3)Harnessed Firestorm Assault: It's a damage booster that also lets you activate charms for free<br /> <br /> (4)Mela's Flashing tongue: If you ever have to go bonfire, this charm is your next choice to activate.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Occult</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (1)Spirit Detecting Mirror Technique: You need this to see dematerialized spirits that may be spying on or trying to kill you.<br /> <br /> (1)Secret Wind Revelation: This will also help you pick out said dematerialized assassins.<br /> <br /> (1)Spirit Grounding Shout: You need this to fight spirits who are dematerialized.<br /> <br /> (1)Hidden Secrets Whisper: The excellency used for getting other charms.<br /> <br /> (1)Seed and Salt Warding: This can be used to ward off ghosts, again not combat but pre-req<br /> <br /> (2)Dragon's Sacred Talon: If you ever need to fight the dead or faeries, this is your charm.<br /> <br /> (3)Spirit Shredding Attack: Used to hurt spirits even more.<br /> <br /> OPTIONAL:<br /> <br /> Terrestrial Circle Sorcery, if you go this route there's any number of spells you can take to improve yourself, like Invulnerable Skin of Bronze for example.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Resistance</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (1)Ox Body Technique: Get five of these.<br /> <br /> (1)Purifying Blood Ascendancy: Resistance excellency, used for resisting poison and environmental effects.<br /> <br /> (1)Body Cleansing Prana: Useful against poisons, which your enemies may use as a tool against you.<br /> <br /> (1)Impervious Skin of Stone: The most basic soak booster, this is useful against powerful attacks that you're not sure you can block or dodge<br /> <br /> (3)Dragon's Unfailing Vigour: Give you even more health levels.<br /> <br /> (3)Fathomless Depths Replenishment: Gain EVEN MORE health levels on the daily.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Which if you tally them all up is about 60 charms, and that's not counting any evocations from your weapon or spells that you might want, but you'll also only reach that point over 300xp into the game. Also yes, occult is for fighting spirits, which you may have to do.<br /> <br /> It's a lot of charms, but if you start taking charms away you're worse at fighting. If you don't have Burning Pinnacle Strike, then there are going to be times where you could have made a bonus attack that you now couldn't. If you don't have Dragon's Unfailing Vigour then you could die by the margin of 2 health levels and it would have saved you theoretically.<br /> <br /> So that's around the top, or close to it, I'm sure I missed some key things. If that's what you want to strive for, then it leaves almost no room for anything else, but you will absolutely be better at fighting than almost anything you ever face. As long as they don't outnumber you anyway, fighting 5 Blood Apes at once is going to suuuuuck. Also I don't actually recommend building your character like this, and if you took 1/3 the charms listed here you'd still be an absolute MONSTER in combat, it's just that you could be better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-11T23:46:37-07:00","id":1330499,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the double post, but I thought I should write something to clarify maybe why this is the case.<br /> <br /> If you look at a lot of fiction stories where the protagonist, or just one of the characters, is the greatest swordsman ever, who can kill any opponent in a single swing so fast you never see the blade leave the scabbard, then in the world of Exalted that would be an exalt, and probably a Solar. The thing is, there's a lot of exalts. So in a Green Arrow story with only Green Arrow you've got a story about a guy who can just churn through bad guys like butter, and then maybe encounters some resistance with the big final guy. In a justice league story though, that's just not happening. Not only is he fighting along side the justice league, which would be totally pointless if Green Arrow could chew through all the bad guys on his own, but the enemies they're facing are so many and so powerful that even superman doesn't want to face them alone.<br /> <br /> The world of Exalted is a lot more like the Justice League than a standalone movie. That goes double for dragonblooded games, since you're still relatively close in power to the most common type of exalt. A good ST will work around that though, again especially for DB games. With only like 4-5 charms if you get stopped by a group of soldiers in the street you can easily kill all of them with a single action and then keep walking along your merry way. It's just that if you're unfortunate enough to get surrounded by 5 DBs and you're alone, then your options are basically run, surrender or die fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T08:40:21-07:00","id":1330552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330499#post1330499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you look at a lot of fiction stories where the protagonist, or just one of the characters, is the greatest swordsman ever, who can kill any opponent in a single swing so fast you never see the blade leave the scabbard, then in the world of Exalted that would be an exalt, and probably a Solar. The thing is, there's a lot of exalts. So in a Green Arrow story with only Green Arrow you've got a story about a guy who can just churn through bad guys like butter, and then maybe encounters some resistance with the big final guy. In a justice league story though, that's just not happening. Not only is he fighting along side the justice league, which would be totally pointless if Green Arrow could chew through all the bad guys on his own, but the enemies they're facing are so many and so powerful that even superman doesn't want to face them alone.<br /> <br /> The world of Exalted is a lot more like the Justice League than a standalone movie. That goes double for dragonblooded games, since you're still relatively close in power to the most common type of exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this:<br /> <br /> If you're playing an Air Aspect Swordsman and your buddy is playing an Earth Aspect Immaculate (with Fist of Titans no less) then you are Green Arrow and they are Superman. You can close that gap if you build your character keeping the idiosyncrasies of the game system in mind.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I'd rather you game the system and min-max to close that gap, because that makes designing encounters easier (especially combat). But it seems your ST comes from a different school of thought.<br /> <br /> Green Arrow is a powerful hero. You basically can't make a bad character in Exalted. But you can easily make a good character who is much worse than all their peers in every area. And that can cause frustration if you expected party balance -- but sometimes changing expectations is better than changing your character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330490#post1330490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Welll...a lot of charms. Here's a basic rundown, I think, of the ones you want for fighting, assuming you want to go with the Fire Aura idea and no artifacts and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great list. I broadly agree (not going to repeat the breakdown I linked to earlier).<br /> <br /> Got a top 15 Essence 2 and below list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-12-2019, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T10:12:49-07:00","id":1330566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1330552#post1330552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Got a top 15 Essence 2 and below list?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm I think that would be extremely difficult just because different synergies, especially outside of a white room. For example if you want to grab Stamina 5 and 5 ox bodies, that\u2019s amazing, you\u2019re more than 3 times as hard to kill. The downside is that if you get knocked down halfway through your -2 health levels it takes 33 days to heal back to full, if you get Wound Closing Touch you can knock that down to something like 6 days. Or what about missing all of your -1s? That\u2019s either 15 days or 2.5 depending on Wound Closing. So if you\u2019re going that route I\u2019d say definitely WCT if you can\u2019t rely on an ally to have it. Also if you\u2019ve got 5 stamina then Impervious Skin of Stone is really good. On the other hand if you\u2019ve only got one stamina ISS is awful and even maxing ox bodies is...well it\u2019s still amazing it\u2019s just less so.<br /> <br /> I find that\u2019s a very Earthy/Woody way of going about things, because then you can use Demon Crushing Wolf Bite really effectively, which is doubly great because with 5 stamina and high dex you probably won\u2019t have a ton left over for strength. For that strategy you probably don\u2019t raise your defence hardly ever, just use ISS to soak high damage attacks, if the enemy gets high initiative that\u2019s okay because unless it\u2019s 40+ you\u2019re not in danger of dying and you can just smack them back harder once they blow all their initiative into a decisive.<br /> <br /> Looking at it from a more Fire perspective Blinding Spark Distraction is very good because it plays so well into the excellency and Flame Borne Interception. Where Earth and Wood are hard and tough, Fire is aggressive and elusive. If you miss your first attack and they blind you with Blinding Spark you can get stuck in an awful death spiral. You\u2019ve likely lost 2 points to your defence, and are at -3 to attack and even to run away, and because of that you\u2019re really likely to just keep feeding the Fire aspect more more discounts and making it easier and easier to blind you. I\u2019m fact, keeping with Fire\u2019s aggression theme, I might even launch a weak decisive after Blinding my opponent in hopes of getting them to their -2s, because when you\u2019re at -5 to all combat actions you\u2019re half-past screwed. That strategy is more fragile than just roughing through things, eventually one flubbed roll or one awesome one will throw a wrench into things, but the reward is worth the risk most of the time. Especially at Essence 3 when you get Pinnacle Strike and Cloud Riot and stuff. Cloud Riot reflexive clash, blind them with Blinding Spark, then reflexive Strike their blind class-penaltied ass.<br /> <br /> For that build though wound closing is way worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T12:11:02-07:00","id":1330589,"title":"","content":"Also just since it\u2019s bugging me being incomplete, air defensive charms do things like give bonus evasion against ranged attacks, give you a disengage bonus in athletics even though disengage is dodge, the archery range extending charms are air aspected not wood, the air brawl signature lets you attack from range...so to me that says air is elusive in a way fire isn\u2019t, where fire is in your face dodging around your attack and making you burn for it, air is keeping at range just out of reach.<br /> <br /> Water on the other hand is dynamic as all hell. They really took the \u201cbe shapeless be formless.\u201d with it. It adds dex to soak, enemy 1s add to soak and hardness and remove attack successes, you gain hardness equal to your current initiative, it\u2019s all over the place. The only real common thing is that it doesn\u2019t usually add static numbers and it goes about things in weird ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-12T14:31:05-07:00","id":1330619,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all of the support. This thread had been incredibly helpful! I'm about to sit down and rework my character as we speak. I'll post what I come up with here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24836-timbo","name":"Timbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24836_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-30T20:55:28-07:00","id":1333344,"title":"","content":"Did no one mention using Dragon-Graced Weapon to bleed off an anima level by making a Melee weapon? It costs four motes and is a reflexive action unto itself, so it doesn't raise your anima back up.<br /> <br /> It's proving rather central to my analysis on how to get the most out of Mirror-on-Water Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T01:49:46-07:00","id":1333365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1333344#post1333344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did no one mention using Dragon-Graced Weapon to bleed off an anima level by making a Melee weapon? It costs four motes and is a reflexive action unto itself, so it doesn't raise your anima back up.<br /> <br /> It's proving rather central to my analysis on how to get the most out of Mirror-on-Water Focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>3m isn't it?<br /> <br /> Bonus points for making a javelin that you can then throw. <br /> <br /> What was the ruling on what an &quot;instant&quot; is? Could you expend a level of anima to make the weapon at the start of your turn then use Elemental Sheath at the end of your turn to spend another level of anima to banish it?<br /> <br /> (Also there's extra -0 levels to have from Aura of Invulnerablity which I'm not sure we discussed when talking about maxing your health levels.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 08-31-2019, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T09:20:19-07:00","id":1333399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1333365#post1333365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3m isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonus points for making a javelin that you can then throw. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And in throwing it, you can afford to break the mote commitment after the attack is over, so you could respire those motes at the end of the round.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What was the ruling on what an &quot;instant&quot; is? </div> </div> </div>I can't point to a ruling at this time, but it HAS to be smaller than a &quot;tick&quot;, which is a moment in which multiple characters with the same Initiative value act at the same time.<br /> <br /> An &quot;instant&quot; seems to refer to an instance of conflict, like a reflexive contest between Stealth and Awareness, or the resolution process of a single attack, several of which can take place within a single tick.<br /> <br /> So, I think &quot;instant&quot; generally refers to a single action, reflexive or otherwise.<br /> <br /> That opens the question of whether the three-step process of clinching (gambit, contest, savaging/throwing if that's what you choose) is a single instant or three separate instants. I think it's three separate instants, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> See, a grapple gambit is an instant like any other gambit. A control roll is an instant like any other contested action. And a savaging or throwing attack is an instant like any other attack.<br /> <br /> Whereas the attack roll and the damage roll of an attack are explicitly part of the resolution process of a single action/instant. All Charms to enhance an attack's damage roll have to be declared at the same time as those that enhance the attack roll, unless the Charm itself disagrees.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you expend a level of anima to make the weapon at the start of your turn then use Elemental Sheath at the end of your turn to spend another level of anima to banish it? </div> </div> </div>I had to really think about this one, but ultimately I would allow it.<br /> <br /> You're committing SIX MOTES to hide an elemental weapon with mundane base traits while also maintaining its existence. If you think that's worth the cost, I'd let you do it. If you wanted to drop it, you could break the commitment to the weapon, which would uniquely break the commitment to Elemental Sheath since the weapon no longer exists to hide.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Also there's extra -0 levels to have from Aura of Invulnerablity which I'm not sure we discussed when talking about maxing your health levels.) </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 08-31-2019, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T09:20:19-07:00","id":1333400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1333365#post1333365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3m isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Bonus points for making a javelin that you can then throw. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And in throwing it, you can afford to break the mote commitment after the attack is over, so you could respire those motes at the end of the round.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What was the ruling on what an &quot;instant&quot; is? </div> </div> </div>I can't point to a ruling at this time, but it HAS to be smaller than a &quot;tick&quot;, which is a moment in which multiple characters with the same Initiative value act at the same time.<br /> <br /> An &quot;instant&quot; seems to refer to an instance of conflict, like a reflexive contest between Stealth and Awareness, or the resolution process of a single attack, several of which can take place within a single tick.<br /> <br /> So, I think &quot;instant&quot; generally refers to a single action, reflexive or otherwise.<br /> <br /> That opens the question of whether the three-step process of clinching (gambit, contest, savaging/throwing if that's what you choose) is a single instant or three separate instants. I think it's three separate instants, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could you expend a level of anima to make the weapon at the start of your turn then use Elemental Sheath at the end of your turn to spend another level of anima to banish it? </div> </div> </div>I had to really think about this one, but ultimately I would allow it.<br /> <br /> You're committing SIX MOTES to hide an elemental weapon with mundane base traits while also maintaining its existence. If you think that's worth the cost, I'd let you do it. If you wanted to drop it, you could break the commitment to the weapon, which would uniquely break the commitment to Elemental Sheath since the weapon no longer exists to hide.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Also there's extra -0 levels to have from Aura of Invulnerablity which I'm not sure we discussed when talking about maxing your health levels.) </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T10:45:49-07:00","id":1333406,"title":"","content":"Yeah you can definitely shed two levels of anima by summoning and banishing. It\u2019s also a good way to do anima control if you want to full excellency your join battle since you can do that out of peripheral and then instantly knock it down to dim again first turn while summoning a decent weapon. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m also in agreement for instances being charm expenditure choices. Any time you have to choose all the charm activations at once is an instance. Even cases like Invulnerable Skin of Stone\u2019s earth aura effect would count as a different instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T13:36:58-07:00","id":1333430,"title":"","content":"Also another thing with that, if you\u2019re not already dual wielding you could use that to form shields or weapons with helpful tags any turn that you already want to ditch an anima level. Example, facing off against a Crane master and forming a flexible weapon, or form a shield so you can flurry a disengage with a full defence/rush, or even just summon another weapon to get a clash bonus. I mean if you\u2019re just using it to shed anima anyway you might as well see if there\u2019s any tags in the game that might help. Bonus points if you want to do something like make a piercing attack against a full defence target so you summon a water spear.<br /> <br /> You\u2019d have to be really on top of your tags to go \u201cah damn I absolutely NEED to crash him this turn, also I\u2019m one anima away from bonfire so I have to shed it so I don\u2019t lose wood aura for my defensive charms, so I\u2019ll summon a wood spear so I can make a piercing attack.\u201d If you\u2019re already trying to be good about controlling your anima levels, like using 4m peripheral when you can and peripheral only when you want to unleash hell it shouldn\u2019t be very often that you need to shed levels. You could be proactive about it and search for appropriate tags whenever you have at least one level to shed and that should open your window of opportunity quite a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 08-31-2019, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T17:12:32-07:00","id":1333456,"title":"","content":"I wish Terrestrial Brawl had such a flexible way to burn anima. Currents Sweep Out to Sea doesn't compare in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T17:49:11-07:00","id":1333460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1333456#post1333456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish Terrestrial Brawl had such a flexible way to burn anima. Currents Sweep Out to Sea doesn't compare in that regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. What about using other abilities? Elemental Bolt Attack can shed anima, if you\u2019re going cross elemental aura to your aspect you may want to dip into lore to be able to change up attacks and shed aura with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T18:53:11-07:00","id":1333467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1333460#post1333460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. What about using other abilities? Elemental Bolt Attack can shed anima, if you\u2019re going cross elemental aura to your aspect you may want to dip into lore to be able to change up attacks and shed aura with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elemental Bolt Attack has a similar problem as Currents Sweep: What if your target is already in range?<br /> <br /> As a grappler, your target might already be at close range, within your grasp. No need for a grapple gambit that reaches out to short range, especially if there's already plenty of water around.<br /> <br /> With Elemental Bolt Attack, spending the anima is just to extend the range from short to medium. If your target is at short or close range, there's no point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragon-Graced Weapon lets you discard your weapon and conjure up something completely different, or lets you conjure up something to throw and then cancel immediately afterwards, if you want. Its flexibility enables so many different strategies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-31T19:57:47-07:00","id":1333476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1333467#post1333467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Bolt Attack has a similar problem as Currents Sweep: What if your target is already in range?<br /> <br /> As a grappler, your target might already be at close range, within your grasp. No need for a grapple gambit that reaches out to short range, especially if there's already plenty of water around.<br /> <br /> With Elemental Bolt Attack, spending the anima is just to extend the range from short to medium. If your target is at short or close range, there's no point.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dragon-Graced Weapon lets you discard your weapon and conjure up something completely different, or lets you conjure up something to throw and then cancel immediately afterwards, if you want. Its flexibility enables so many different strategies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it\u2019s true that you don\u2019t need to extend the range most of the time, I imagine it\u2019s something you can do anyway. Although yeah it\u2019s just not that good, in either case you\u2019re forced into a specific combat action and because the charms are simple and supplemental you\u2019re likely to go over 4m in that combat action anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T02:56:11-07:00","id":1390740,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bit of a necro, but I think it's appropriate here.<br /> <br /> How do the new charms in Heirs change the viability of an Air-aspected swordswoman? What charms would you recommend?<br /> <br /> In my 3rd Age game, one main antagonist to the PCs is the Shogun of Iscomay, whose Clan Tepet Dragonblood unofficially rule that Empire with an iron fist. So lots of Air-Aspected spearwomen and swordswomen.<br /> <br /> Here's an example of an NPC I used before, now she's going up to Essence 4 because it's 100 years since they last faced her. I want to buff her up a lot, but keep the fight simple (and so stay in Air aura, not switch between that and fire) and keep her style of fighting with a spear (rather than having her switch to sorcery or something) and maybe throwing ice-javelins a bit when the enemy is at range.<br /> Charm recommendations? I'll probably buff up her stats as well, of course, her attributes are basically starting stats, and she could do with some ox-bodies and stuff.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u><b>Shozei Tepet Hatsuno, \u201cFlashing Spear Lioness\u201d, Air spearwoman, Essence 3.</b></u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Strength 3, Dexterity 5, Stamina 3, Perception 3, Int 3, Wits 3</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Awareness 3, Athletics 4, Melee 5 (+1 Spear), Dodge 4, Resistance 3, War 3, Lore 3, Thrown 5 (+1 Javelins), Integrity 3.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Join Battle 6</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Jade Direlance: Attack 12 dice (17 damage, Overwhelming 5, reaching, can make Piercing attacks). +2 extra dice when clashing.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Jade Direlance: Decisive Attack 11 dice. +2 extra dice when clashing.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Icicle-Javelin throw at short range: Withering attack 14 dice (12 damage, Overwhelming 1, can make Piercing attacks. Enemies who take decisive damage from it take a -1 penalty to all actions until their next turn)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Parry 7 Evasion 5 Soak 8 Hardness 4 (Jade Chain Shirt)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Guile 3 Resolve 3</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Willpower 5</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Personal Essence 14/14</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Peripheral Essence 26/35 </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Health levels: <span style=\"color:#000000\">0/-1/-1/-1/-2/-2/-2/-4/Incap</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Weapon charms:</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Dragon-Grace Weapon</b> (3m, reflexive. Create and ready an icicle-javelin.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Awareness charms: </u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Precision Observation Method</b> (Excellency.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Melee charms:</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Stoking Bonfire Style</b> (Excellency. If hit or parry, reduce cost by 1 vs that opponent for rest of scene. Stacks. Lost if attack/parry another enemy or miss/fail to parry.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Steel Tempest Strike</b> (Once/scene, need to have used an Air charm on a previous action. 4m, 1wp. Use your move action to move forward, ignoring difficult terrain and can even cross chasms or pits, and make a free attack. This can be before or after your normal attack. Reset by gaining 15i in a single tick.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Defence charms:</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Stoking Bonfire Style</b> (Excellency. If hit or parry, reduce cost by 1 vs that opponent for rest of scene. Stacks. Lost if attack/parry another enemy or miss/fail to parry.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Air Anima</b> (For three motes, the Air Aspect may deflect projectiles with a gust of wind, imposing a \u22121 environmental penalty on all ranged attacks against her until her next turn. )<br /> <br /> <u>Ranged charms:</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Seeking Throw Technique</b> (excellency, ignore 1pt of cover or 2 if you aimed.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>Movement charms:</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman, serif\"><b>Air Anima </b>(5m, she can use her reflexive move action to leap an entire range band vertically or horizontally without needing to roll, and suffers no falling damage for the rest of the round. At bonfire, this power is free.)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Effortlessly Rising Flame</b> (Add 1 or 2 successes for 2m each, also roll an extra non-charm dice for each 10)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Bellows Pumping Stride</b> (3m, on a rush roll an extra dice for each 1 the enemy rolled. Disrupts Steel Tempest Strike. )</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Soaring Leap Technique</b> (1m, re-roll a non-1 dice for each 10 you got on a jump, including rush and disengages with a jump stunt)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Incense Smoke Ladder</b> (4m, reflexive. You can run up vertical walls or even upside down. But you can't withdraw or disengage.)</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><u>War charms:</u></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Tactics Mean Everything </b>(excellency, re-roll 6s)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 05-22-2020, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T04:47:47-07:00","id":1390749,"title":"","content":"Flagging the work of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a>, if you're going all-out, then saying Shining Ice Mirror is (a) resonant with DBs (has that ever been queried with the Devs?) (b) re-skinning it as a spear and (c) picking up the Air melee charms in Heirs gets you:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1378370-good-db-builds?p=1378505#post1378505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every time you Aim with Shining Ice mirror, you gain +2 non-Charm defense.<br /> <br /> Cold Moon Slash lets you attack from Medium if you Aimed.<br /> <br /> Long range.<br /> Turn 1: Aim. Get +2 Defense, +3 to hit.<br /> Enemy moves to Medium.<br /> Turn 2: Attack out to Medium range, inflicting mobility penalties and reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll (Unerring Lightning Razor). Wound Penalties on foe.<br /> Enemy moves to Short.<br /> Turn 3: Steel Tempest Strike allows a free Reflexive attack. Ice Fixing Strike Stacks a -1 Defense. Then your actual turn. Unerring Lightning Razor with Willpower for the extra +2 non-Charm defense and reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll (remembering the increased penalty from Cold Moon Slash). Winter Night Cut for another -1 Defense and -2 on attacks.<br /> Enemy attacks you (at -2, -Wound Penalties, at +2 Defense).<br /> Turn 4: Unerring Lightning Razor + Fulminating Thunderclap Surge gives you an Unblockable, -4 (-2 Defense, -2 Mobility, -? Wound) Evasion, attack with +3 dice to hit and damage, reroll (Essence+mobility penalty) failures on attack and damage roll.<br /> <br /> There is no Turn 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Give her Mela's Coils on top of that and she'd likely be very Air and pretty terrifying.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> On the less gonzo/re-skinning an artefact end of the spectrum, other things from Heirs include Flying Dagger Leap (p.131 - looks like it works well with aiming and then leaping into close range) and combining the Air and Earth (if you stick with the dire lance, another aspect if you don't) variants of Dragon-Scale Shield (p.149 - effectively gives you +2 non-charm bonus to your parry and doesn't mess with your aura if you stack Air with something else).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-22-2020, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T04:52:55-07:00","id":1390750,"title":"","content":"I think that the repurchase of unerring lightning razor, which requires first getting unerring lightning razor and Oncoming storm stance, looks pretty great, You get a cap breaker with re-rolls for both attack and damage and, in air aura, you can aim reflexively to break your cap further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T05:15:56-07:00","id":1390752,"title":"","content":"I already have another Air-aspect with Shining Ice Mirror, so I'll be doing that with a different character (who's not here, because she didn't have a lover killed by one of the PCs in the past like this one did).<br /> <br /> I'll look at those charms, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T05:25:13-07:00","id":1390755,"title":"","content":"Disaster! Her nemesis PC wears a buff jacket of thick leather, not metal armour. Still, if he brings his friends in metal armour, maybe she can use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T06:00:09-07:00","id":1390757,"title":"","content":"A few more then I'll pipe down (and assuming you're going to pick up all the Air melee stuff anyways)...<br /> <br /> Dodge has some nice ones: Nimble Zephyr Defence (p.137) in particular.<br /> <br /> Dragon-Graced Rainment (p.155) would mean you could upgrade her to medium armour and not have a mobility penalty, or stick with light armour and get a bonus if you were thinking of making her a 'striking swiftly from the shadows' type and buying up stealth charms.<br /> <br /> If the latter, then Blood-Chilling Strike (p.159) might be useful.<br /> <br /> If she commands an archer battlegroup, then Swift Rain, Fierce Storm (p.161) would help.<br /> <br /> Lastly, if she fights alongside other DBs, then Victory-Seeking Insight (p.131), Tiger-and-Dragon Combination and Twin Dragons Dancing (p.162) feel like gamechangers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 05-22-2020, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T08:40:14-07:00","id":1390780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1330104-help-building-an-air-aspected-melee-focused?p=1390755#post1390755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disaster! Her nemesis PC wears a buff jacket of thick leather, not metal armour.</div> </div> </div> </div>She can still get re-rolls equal to her essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I want to play <a href=\"https://forum.atlas-games.com/t/adelbert-a-magi-of-hermes-look-at-intellego-and-astrology/8146/382\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> as a starting character, I don't even care what game.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/872-apromor","name":"Apromor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T09:06:03-07:00","id":1390793,"title":"